    "created_at": "2022-09-25T10:33:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-09-25T10:33:17Z",
    "body": "> This does not just apply in A1 -> B -> A2 scenarios (though there too A2 might not want A1 to think it wasn't influenced by B), but also in A -> B -> C scenarios. C shouldn't think the authority is A when it's really a mix of A and B.\r\n\r\nThis issue also applies to A -> B -> C.\r\nIn TAO, unlike CORS, B doesn't have any influence over C. The only thing exposed is timing of a resource from C, and it's only exposed to A. How can B affect the timing in a way that would make C expose something that it doesn't want to A?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
